  "summary": "Lightwell Security Advisory: waitress 2.0.0+rhlw.1",
  "details": "Red Hat Lightwell has released waitress 2.0.0+rhlw.1 with backported fixes for CVE-2022-24761, CVE-2024-49769, and CVE-2024-49768.\n\nCVE-2022-24761: HTTP Request Smuggling in waitress\n\nCVE-2024-49769: Waitress has a denial of service leading to high CPU usage/resource exhaustion\n\nCVE-2024-49768: Waitress has request processing race condition in HTTP pipelining with invalid first request\n\nThis patched artifact is a drop-in replacement for waitress 2.0.0 from PyPI.",
